  "description": "Post-quantum integration for ASP.NET Core Identity, with two surfaces at deliberately different maturity profiles. (1) PRODUCTION-READY Argon2id password hashing — PHC-formatted, secure-by-default work factors, transparent rehash-on-login, one-line PBKDF2→Argon2id migration via AddArgon2idPasswordHasherWithMigration, fail-closed verification, RFC 9106 §5.3 Known Answer Tests + reference-CLI PHC interop + emitter wire-format pin. Runs on net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0. (2) PREVIEW hybrid post-quantum JWT issuance for owned/trusted ecosystems — ML-DSA-65 signatures (FIPS 204) with optional X-Wing (X25519 + ML-KEM-768) encryption, kid-based key rotation, JSON-source-gen claim path. Uses non-IANA algorithm identifiers; intentionally not interoperable with generic JWT tooling. Requires .NET 10 (and OpenSSL 3.5+ on Linux). Supply chain: every .nupkg ships with an embedded CycloneDX SBOM, GitHub Sigstore-signed build-provenance attestation (verifiable with gh attestation verify), deterministic SourceLink builds, .snupkg symbols, CodeQL on every PR, Dependabot. Not yet independently audited. See https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity for the production-readiness stance, the Roadmap to 1.0, the migration guide, and runnable minimal-API + MVC samples.",
