  "releaseNotes": "0.6.0-preview.1 — Verify-path hardening, full owned-ecosystem sample lifecycle, trusted publishing.\n\nSecurity (one behavior change, in the fail-closed direction):\n  - PHC verification acceptance bounds: a poisoned stored row can no longer\n    demand an absurd Argon2id computation (m=2147483647 was a ~2 TiB\n    allocation attempt per verify). Accepted: m in [8 KiB, 4 GiB],\n    t in [1, 512], p in [1, 64] (m >= 8p), salt in [8, 64] B,\n    tag in [12, 512] B. Out-of-range fails closed before any allocation.\n  - Canonicality pins: exactly one accepted spelling per hash — canonical\n    unpadded base64 for salt/tag (whitespace + trailing-bit aliases\n    rejected), no leading-zero numeric aliases, and oversized fields\n    rejected on length before any decode work.\n  - Argon2idOptions.Validate() gains matching upper bounds so the emitter\n    can never produce a hash its own verifier refuses.\n  - BREAKING if you ever ran an out-of-range config (e.g.\n    DegreeOfParallelism above 64): stored hashes from such configs no\n    longer verify and there is no automatic recovery — read the CHANGELOG\n    and docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md before upgrading.\n  - New deterministic generative (fuzz-style) corpus for the PHC parser;\n    acceptance bounds pinned at both edges of every axis.\n\nSamples — the full provision → issue → verify → rotate lifecycle:\n  - NEW Verifier.Demo: a separate resource service validating tokens across\n    a real process boundary with only public keys (no Identity, no\n    passwords, no private keys). The \"you own both the issuer and every\n    verifier\" topology, runnable.\n  - NEW KeyTool: generate/inspect ML-DSA-65 keys as (optionally encrypted)\n    PKCS#8 + SPKI PEM. Pure BCL, zero dependencies.\n  - Issuer demo can now load KeyTool-provisioned keys (PQ_ISSUER_KEY_DIR).\n  - .http walkthrough files for all three web samples.\n\nDocs: NEW docs/QUANTUM-READINESS.md (what to do about the quantum threat,\nin what order) and docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md (symptom → cause → fix).\n\nInfrastructure: NuGet Trusted Publishing (no long-lived API key),\nArgon2id benchmarks in CI with a regression budget, macOS discovery lane.\n\nStill preview — NOT independently audited. See KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
